Usages:
  action_set: |
    Recognized relabel actions (validated at parse time, executed by ParsedConfigs.Apply):
    replace (default), replace_all, keep, drop, keep_if_contains, drop_if_contains,
    keep_if_equal, drop_if_equal, keepequal, dropequal, hashmod, labelmap, labelmap_all,
    labeldrop, labelkeep, uppercase, lowercase, graphite. keep_metrics/drop_metrics are accepted
    at parse time and rewritten internally to keep/drop against the __name__ label.

Annotations: |
  This cell is a pure, side-effect-free label-transformation engine implementing Prometheus
  relabeling semantics (plus VictoriaMetrics extensions like keep_if_contains/hashmod/keepequal)
  over slices of label pairs. It is the single implementation shared by every ingestion surface:
  the scrape path (lib/promscrape) and the push/remote-write path (via app/vminsert's and
  app/vmagent's own relabel wrapper packages) both compile YAML relabel rules through this
  cell's loaders and execute the same `ParsedConfigs` Apply logic, guaranteeing byte-for-byte
  identical relabeling behavior regardless of which component or wire protocol samples entered
  through.

  Use `action_set` when implementing or reasoning about a new relabel rule's runtime behavior.

---

"RelabelConfig(if: IfExpression, action: string, sourceLabels: []string, separator: string, targetLabel: string, regex: string, modulus: uint64, replacement: string)":
  location: config.go
  annotations: |
    Raw, YAML-shaped form of one relabel rule, as written by a user in a scrape config or
    remote-write relabel config file.

    `action`: one of `action_set`; validated and normalized at parse time
    `if`: optional `IfExpression` gating whether this rule applies to a given label set
    Requirements:
    - Must be compiled via `ParseRelabelConfigs` before it can be applied; this raw form is
      never applied directly

"ParsedConfigs()":
  location: relabel.go
  annotations: |
    Compiled, ready-to-execute form of an ordered list of `RelabelConfig` rules. Obtained via
    `LoadRelabelConfigs`, `ParseRelabelConfigsData`, or `ParseRelabelConfigs`; never constructed
    directly.
  methods:
    "Len() -> count:int": |
      Number of compiled rules.
    "String() -> text:string": |
      Render back to a human-readable form (used for debug endpoints).
    "Apply(labels: []Label, labelsOffset: int) -> labels:[]Label": |
      Apply every compiled rule in order to `labels` starting at `labelsOffset`, returning the
      transformed label slice. This is the hot-path entry point called once per scraped/ingested
      sample.

      `labelsOffset`: index marking where this sample's own labels start (labels before the
      offset are treated as shared/external labels not subject to source_labels lookups)
    "ApplyDebug(labels: []Label) -> labels:[]Label, steps:[]DebugStep": |
      Same as this type's own Apply method, but additionally records one `DebugStep` per rule
      for troubleshooting endpoints (e.g. why a target/metric was dropped or relabeled a
      particular way).

"DebugStep(rule: string, in: string, out: string)":
  location: relabel.go
  annotations: |
    One recorded relabeling step: the rule text, the label set before (`in`) and after (`out`)
    applying it. Purely a debug-endpoint artifact, never used on the hot path.
  methods:
    "String() -> text:string": |
      Human-readable rendering of this step.

"IfExpression()":
  location: if_expression.go
  annotations: |
    A boolean matcher over a label set, compiled from either a PromQL/MetricsQL-style series
    selector string or a metric-expression AST. Used to gate whether a `RelabelConfig` rule
    applies to a given sample.
  methods:
    "Parse(s: string) -> err:error": |
      Compile `s` (a series-selector-like string, e.g. `{env="prod"}`) into matchable form.
    "ParseFromMetricExpr(me: MetricExpr) -> err:error": |
      Compile from an already-parsed metric expression AST instead of raw text.
    "Match(labels: []Label) -> matched:bool": |
      Evaluate whether `labels` satisfies this expression.
    "String() -> text:string": |
      Render back to its original selector-like text form.

"LoadRelabelConfigs(path: string) -> parsed:ParsedConfigs, raw:[]byte, err:error":
  location: config.go
  annotations: |
    Read and compile a relabel-config YAML file from disk.

    `raw`: the unparsed file bytes, kept for debug/reload-diffing endpoints

"ParseRelabelConfigsData(data: []byte) -> parsed:ParsedConfigs, err:error":
  location: config.go
  annotations: |
    Parse and compile relabel configs from in-memory YAML bytes (used when config arrives via
    HTTP or is embedded rather than read from a local file).

"ParseRelabelConfigs(rcs: []RelabelConfig) -> parsed:ParsedConfigs, err:error":
  location: config.go
  annotations: |
    Compile an already-YAML-decoded slice of `RelabelConfig` into a `ParsedConfigs`.

    Algorithm:
    1. Validate and normalize each rule's action against `action_set`
    2. Compile each rule's source_labels/regex/if into matchable form
    3. Reject the whole set on the first invalid rule, returning an error

"FinalizeLabels(dst: []Label, src: []Label) -> labels:[]Label":
  location: relabel.go
  annotations: |
    Append `src` onto `dst` while resolving name collisions and dropping labels with empty
    values, producing the final label set for a sample after all relabeling has run.

"GetLabelByName(labels: []Label, name: string) -> label:Label":
  location: relabel.go
  annotations: |
    Find the label named `name` in `labels`, or a nil/zero result if absent.

"SanitizeLabelName(name: string) -> name:string":
  location: relabel.go
  annotations: |
    Replace characters not valid in a Prometheus label name with an underscore.

"SanitizeMetricName(value: string) -> name:string":
  location: relabel.go
  annotations: |
    Replace characters not valid in a Prometheus metric name with an underscore.

"GetScrapeURL(labels: Labels, extraParams: map[string][]string) -> url:string, path:string":
  location: scrape_url.go
  annotations: |
    Build the final scrape URL for a target from its (post-relabeling) label set — combining
    the __address__/__scheme__/__metrics_path__ meta-labels with any extra query
    parameters configured for the job.

